<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Sovereign Principality of the United Netherlands</h1><p class="st-meta">1813 CE – 1815 CE · capital Amsterdam</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The transitional Dutch state of 1813–1815, created as Napoleon's empire collapsed, under the returning Prince of Orange as sovereign prince.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>, French authority in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> collapsed in November 1813. A provisional government led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gijsbert-karel-van-hogendorp">Gijsbert Karel van Hogendorp</a> invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-the-netherlands">William Frederick</a>, son of the last stadtholder, to return. He landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheveningen">Scheveningen</a> on 30 November and accepted the title of sovereign prince.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>William ruled under a new constitution adopted in 1814, which gave the sovereign wide powers while keeping a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/states-general-of-the-netherlands">States General</a>. The new state rejected the old federal republic in favour of the unitary government created in the Batavian period. Its priority was rebuilding finances and securing allied backing at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The great powers decided to unite the northern and southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> as a barrier to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In March 1815, during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>, William proclaimed himself king, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-kingdom-of-the-netherlands">United Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sovereign-principality-of-the-united-netherlands.jpg" alt="Sovereign Principality of the United Netherlands" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1813 CE – 1815 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Amsterdam</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William I of the Netherlands, Gijsbert Karel van Hogendorp</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Calvinism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Soevereine Vorstendom der Verenigde Nederlanden</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=sovereign-principality-of-the-united-netherlands" aria-label="Sovereign Principality of the United Netherlands on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4790 370 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sovereign Principality of the United Netherlands lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5110 626L5054 728M5110 626L5110 626"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5110 626h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5110 626h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5110 626h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Amsterdam. <a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=sovereign-principality-of-the-united-netherlands">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
